 "notes": "Strip d (x 5400-7500, overlap 5100-7800) of 22-38. Clifton Avenue is straight: centre x~6319 (60 ft, lines ~6271/6367) north of Ludlow, ~6322 south of Ludlow where it is 100 ft (6245-6403) along Burnet Woods; the inner lines in Clifton are water pipes and the street railway, not kerbs. House numbers are printed inside the street lines. Names as printed: WOOLPER, McALPIN, RESOR, THRALL ST., SHILO ST., BRYANT (AVE.), TELFORD (with AVE. printed further north on the same street), LORAINE ... ST., GLENMARY ... AVE., INTERWOOD AVE., BIDDLE ST., BROOKLINE (no suffix on this strip; written Brookline Avenue as on the 1904 sheets), SENATOR ... PL., HOSEA ... AVE., HOWELL, TERRACE, ORMOND AVE. (1904 sheets wrote Ormond Street), DIXMYTH. Ludlow/Dixmyth labels are off-strip; taken from the plate. Big spaced lettering (H. WOOD, ...WOODS EST., COOK'S, BRYANT'S, B.B. WHITEMAN'S EST., WHITEMAN & BUTLERS, ...LEY'S, ...HOTEL'S, WEST, STERLING) is subdivision/owner text, not streets. Dixmyth's south side is the plate clip; its centreline is taken 41 px (27.5 ft) in from the north lot fronts. Clifton runs off the plate at y~5420 (plate edge, not an end). Not picked (beyond the 300 px overlap): Hosea/Brookline (~7900,3600, Hosea jogs there), Ludlow/Jefferson, Glenmary east of Biddle, and the unnamed avenue's west end at the N-S avenue x~4920."
}